            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0461" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5011: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-09-01T16:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 2—12:17
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>222. President Diaz has just shown me a curt telegram of resignation from
                    Chamorro, presumably called forth by the telegrams referred <pb facs="0462"
                        n="360" xml:id="pg360"/> to in my telegram of August 31, 3 p.m. It is not
                    known how this will affect Chamorro’s declared intention of leaving Europe for
                    Nicaragua via the United States about September 14th.</p>
                <p>Diaz has replied requesting explanation of the ex-President’s reasons for
                    resignation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
